<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρουργ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of technical dexterity,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ χ. ἐπιστήμη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1341b1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μὴ χ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν τεχνῶν</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				5.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. μέρος τῆς μουσικῆς</span>
			the <i>practical</i> part of music, i.e. <i>execution,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1135d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>for surgery,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>surgery,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				3.85
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					2.148
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>worked by hand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hero
					<u>Bel.</u>
					75.5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
